  abstract = {We consider the problem of optimal quadratures for integrandsf: [-1,1]{\textrightarrow}? which have an analytic extension\$\${\textbackslash}bar f\$\$to an open diskDrof radiusr about the origin such that\$\${\textbackslash}left{\textbar} \{{\textbackslash}bar f\} {\textbackslash}right{\textbar}\$\$?1 on\$\${\textbackslash}bar D\_r \$\$. Ifr=1, we show that the penalty for sampling the integrand at zeros of the Legendre polynomial of degreen rather than at optimal points, tends to infinity withn. In particular there is an {\textquotedblleft}infinite{\textquotedblright} penalty for using Gauss quadrature. On the other hand, ifr{\textgreater}1, Gauss quadrature is almost optimal. These results hold for both the worst-case and asymptotic settings.},
